      "evidence": ["No memory includes temporal normalization (e.g., 'last week' → March 20–26, 2023), speaker-annotated role labels, or abstractive summaries; all are raw, unstructured, and ungrounded text snippets with no auxiliary signals for QA reasoning."]
    }
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "skill_change": "Implement adaptive memory segmentation with semantic boundary detection",
      "concrete_action": "Replace fixed-length truncation with sentence- and clause-aware chunking (e.g., using spaCy sentence boundaries + discourse connectives) to ensure each stored memory is a complete, self-contained utterance or proposition — preserving temporal adverbials, subjects, predicates, and objects."
    },
    {
      "skill_change": "Introduce multi-stage retrieval with query-aware re-ranking",
      "concrete_action": "Augment retrieval with: (1) question-type classification (temporal / entity / inference), (2) temporal cue extraction from question ('when', 'first', '2019'), and (3) re-ranker that scores memory chunks by temporal modifier overlap (e.g., 'last week', 'yesterday', '2019') and named entity co-occurrence (e.g., 'Eternal Sunshine' ↔ 'Joanna' ↔ 'watched')."
    },
    {
      "skill_change": "Enrich memory storage with structured metadata and lightweight grounding",
      "concrete_action": "For each stored memory, auto-annotate: (a) absolute timestamp (if available in session context or inferred from external anchor), (b) normalized temporal expressions ('last week' → ISO date range), (c) speaker ID + role (e.g., 'Caroline: supporter/advocate'), and (d) inferred intent/domain tags (e.g., 'LGBTQ support group' → [domain: counseling, intent: professional development])."
    }
  ]
}

